{title: It Is Well with My Soul}
{lyricist: Horatio G. Spafford, 1873}
{composer: VILLE DU HAVRE, Philip P. Bliss, 1876}
{copyright: Public domain}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 76}

{start_of_verse}
When [C]peace, like a [F]river, at[C]tendeth my way,
When [Am]sorrows like [D7]sea billows [G]roll;
What[C]ever my [F]lot, Thou hast [C]taught me to [Am]say,
It is [C/G]well, it is [G7]well with my [C]soul.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]It is well (it is [C]well)
With my [G]soul (with my [C]soul),
It is [F]well, it is [C/G]well with [G7]my [C]soul.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
Though [C]Satan should [F]buffet, though [C]trials should come,
Let [Am]this blest as[D7]surance con[G]trol,
That [C]Christ has re[F]garded my [C]helpless es[Am]tate,
And hath [C/G]shed His own [G7]blood for my [C]soul.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
My [C]sin, oh, the [F]bliss of this [C]glorious thought!
My [Am]sin, not in [D7]part but the [G]whole,
Is [C]nailed to the [F]cross, and I [C]bear it no [Am]more,
Praise the [C/G]Lord, praise the [G7]Lord, O my [C]soul!
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
And, [C]Lord, haste the [F]day when my [C]faith shall be sight,
The [Am]clouds be rolled [D7]back as a [G]scroll;
The [C]trump shall re[F]sound, and the [C]Lord shall de[Am]scend,
Even [C/G]so, it is [G7]well with my [C]soul.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
